  "summary": "The youngest Russian lacquer school: Palekh-born masters painting cool lyric landscapes on black boxes.",
  "description": "Mstyora's icon painters, denied their trade, founded a lacquer miniature artel in 1931, learning from Palekh but splitting stylistically: cooler palettes, broad lyrical landscapes, architecture lovingly drawn, and icon-like harmony across larger fields. Scenes of village festivals, legends and wartime heroism sit on black lacquer with restrained gold, bridging icon tradition and Soviet narrative painting. The Mstyora museum houses the school's canonical works, and its workshops remain one of Russia's four lacquer miniature centers.",
